  "content": "Peer interactive result language (trusted catalog rules; not runtime authority).\nLibrary peer-basic-1; specHash sha256:051318a0dd98fde6c372a3929e8c2eaff02c513f8f2f773a7f036b5c852315f5.\nPublish only if publish_interactive_result is projected to this worker. Inspectors never gain publish rights. This is a fixed snapshot, not a live website.\nDSL: one name=expression per line; root=component is required. Component arguments are positional in the order below; optional trailing arguments may be omitted. Arrays use [], objects use {key:value}. Use references by name. State defaults are $name=finiteNumber|string|boolean literals; use $name directly in each input value position. Never quote a state binding.\nFunctions use @Name(args). Operators: + - * / % == != > < >= <= && || ! and ternary ?:; numeric operands must be numbers, never divide/modulo by zero. No loops, recursion, dynamic functions, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, URLs, imports, Query, Mutation, MCP, network, Now or Random. Only the names below exist.\nkey means /^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_-]{0,63}$/. All numbers are finite IEEE754; specify units. Decimal uses 0..6 decimal places. Layout children contain only registered elements. IDs and table row keys must be stable and unique. Chart xKey values are unique; series values are numeric.\nComponents:\nCol(children:JSON[0..300]) — Vertical layout.\nRow(children:JSON[0..300]) — Responsive horizontal layout.\nCard(title:string[1..160],children:JSON[0..300]) — Titled group.\nTitle(text:string[0..8192]) — Result heading.\nText(text:string[0..8192]) — Plain factual or explanatory text.\nCaption(text:string[0..8192]) — Supporting plain text.\nDivider() — Section separator.\nMetric(label:string[1..160],value:string[0..8192]|number,unit?:string[0..32]) — Labeled number or text, with explicit unit.\nTable(label:string[1..160],columns:{key:key,label:string[1..160]}[1..20],rows:JSON[0..500],rowKey:key) — Bounded table with local pagination.\nChart(label:string[1..160],kind:\"bar\"|\"line\",xKey:key,series:{key:key,label:string[1..160]}[1..6],rows:JSON[0..500]) — Bounded bar or line chart with equivalent data table.\nInput(id:key,label:string[1..160],value:string[0..8192]) — Labeled text state binding.\nNumberInput(id:key,label:string[1..160],value:number,min:number,max:number,step:number>0) — Labeled finite numeric state binding; min/max/positive step.\nSelect(id:key,label:string[1..160],value:string[0..8192],options:{value:string[0..8192],label:string[1..160]}[1..100]) — Labeled local selection from declared options.\nCheckbox(id:key,label:string[1..160],value:boolean) — Labeled boolean state binding.\nSlider(id:key,label:string[1..160],value:number,min:number,max:number,step:number>0) — Labeled bounded numeric state binding.\nButton(label:string[1..160],action:LocalAction) — Local @Set or @Reset action only.\nSourceReference(bindingId:key,label:string[1..160]) — Source for an admitted literal bindingId; never a URL or path.\nPure functions (bounded rows, own fields only):\n@Data(bindingId:key) -> JSON — Read an admitted immutable data binding by literal bindingId.\n@RowsWhere(rows:JSON[0..500],field:key,comparison:\"eq\"|\"ne\"|\"gt\"|\"gte\"|\"lt\"|\"lte\"|\"contains\",value:string[0..8192]|number|boolean|null) -> JSON[0..500] — Filter finite rows by own field, comparison eq/ne/gt/gte/lt/lte/contains and scalar value.\n@Total(rows:JSON[0..500],field:key) -> number — Sum finite numeric own-field values. Missing/non-numeric values are errors.\n@RowCount(rows:JSON[0..500]) -> number — Count the bounded rows actually provided.\n@GroupTotals(rows:JSON[0..500],groupField:key,valueField:key) -> JSON[0..500] — Group bounded rows by a scalar own field and sum a numeric field. Returns group and total rows.\n@Decimal(value:number,places:integer[0..6]) -> string[0..8192] — Format a finite value with 0-6 decimal places; no implicit currency or locale.\nLocalAction: @Set($declaredState,expression), @Reset($declaredState,...), or @Action([these actions]). Set/Reset cannot call tools, send messages, write project files or modify data bindings. Do not use permission/grant/evidence/taskstatus/executionstatus/accepted/approval as state names.\nLimits: program 64KiB; fallback 32KiB; input snapshots total 512KiB, <=16 bindings; AST <=1000 nodes/depth24; expanded elements <=300/depth12; state <=64 fields/64KiB; strings <=8192 chars; collections <=500; table <=20 columns, local pages <=100 rows/1000 cells; chart <=6 series/500 total points. Pure evaluation has a shared 40000-step budget; do not multiply expensive nested computations.\nMaterials: copy the host interactiveMaterial.source from actual Tool Results and choose bounded payload/json fields/rows. @Data requires an existing literal bindingId. Keep exact source version/classification/redaction/truncation; no file reread, preview padding or fabricated Evidence. model-data is always an assumption/example. Missing canonical data requires an ordinary governed read or honest text fallback.\nPublication: explicit create, or revise with an admitted owner/resultId/contentVersion base. Same call ID always has identical parameters; use a new ID only for a known noncommitted corrected candidate. At most two content repairs after the initial validation failure, within the original work budget. Pending/unknown means inspect the original publication target, never replay with another ID. Version conflict never auto-rebases or creates a substitute result.\ninspect_interactive_result: main Bot metadata/text only; worker/Verifier may read fixed program, selected bindings and bounded evaluation. Evaluation uses validated initial values, or an explicitly admitted frozen user followup; never latest UI state. Publish/read/compute Evidence proves those operations, not source business truth, verification or acceptance.\nExample (model assumption; inputs=[]):\n$budget=100\nroot=Col([Title(\"Estimate\"),NumberInput(\"budget\",\"Budget\",$budget,0,10000,1),Metric(\"Double\",$budget*2,\"USD\"),Button(\"Reset\",@Reset($budget))])"
